## 2) How to use it

### Example: save 4 models + their dataframes (explicit mapping)

```r
out <- save_model_bundle(
  model_names = c("full_model_A", "full_model_B", "full_model_C", "full_model_D"),
  model_data_map = c(
    full_model_A = "A",
    full_model_B = "B",
    full_model_C = "C",
    full_model_D = "D"
  ),
  bundle_path = "housing_models_bundle.rds",
  manifest_csv_path = "housing_models_manifest.csv",
  format = "rds"
)
```

### If your `lm()` calls use `data = A` etc., you can omit `model_data_map`

It will try to infer `A` from `model$call$data`:

```r
out <- save_model_bundle(
  model_names = c("full_model_A", "full_model_B"),
  bundle_path = "bundle.rds",
  manifest_csv_path = "manifest.csv"
)
```

### Include extra dataframes not directly tied to a model

```r
out <- save_model_bundle(
  model_names = c("m1", "m2"),
  data_names = c("df_lookup", "df_test"),
  bundle_path = "bundle.rds",
  manifest_csv_path = "manifest.csv"
)
```

