## Recommendation

* If `garagespaces` can be 0 (it can), the best modeling choice is to **define** `ln_garagespaces = log1p(garagespaces)` and refit. You can keep the formula unchanged by keeping the same column name.
* If you can’t refit right now, use **training-median imputation** (Strategy B). It avoids introducing a fake “1 garage” effect.

