## How to get from “a list of functions” (e.g., an `.rds`) into a package

If you literally have a list like `funs <- readRDS("my_funs.rds")` where each element is a function object, you *can* convert them into `.R` files — but you’ll lose comments unless you kept them elsewhere.

A practical approach:

### A) Source from your existing `.R` files instead (best)

If your functions already exist in one or more `.R` files: just copy those files into `R/` and add roxygen.

### B) If you only have function objects in a list, write them out

This will write one file per function (you can then consolidate + add docs):

```r
write_functions_to_package <- function(funs, pkg_path, r_dir = "R") {
  dir.create(file.path(pkg_path, r_dir), recursive = TRUE, showWarnings = FALSE)

  for (nm in names(funs)) {
    fn <- funs[[nm]]
    stopifnot(is.function(fn))

    # deparse to text
    txt <- paste0(nm, " <- ", paste(deparse(fn), collapse = "\n"))
    out_file <- file.path(pkg_path, r_dir, paste0(nm, ".R"))
    writeLines(txt, out_file)
  }
}
```

Then:

```r
funs <- readRDS("my_funs.rds")
write_functions_to_package(funs, "~/path/to/codtools")
```

After that, you still need to add roxygen docs + `devtools::document()`.

